    "updated_at": "2022-05-03T02:33:17Z",
    "body": "Thanks, your assessment makes sense to me now. What I wasn’t catching here at all is that insertion isn’t a prepare-a-script trigger for parser-inserted script elements. The element wouldn’t even have text content yet at that point (and this state can be observed with custom element reactions). Instead it’s called when [the text insertion mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-main-incdata) reaches an appropriate end tag token.\r\n\r\nThe steps there begin by explicitly flushing pending microtasks. That would include the queued mutation observer reactions and both the script element and its original parser-inserted text would be available for manipulation at that point. Therefore your earlier suspicion that “the callbacks are executed just before #prepare-a-script” was totally correct.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
